+# GCP catalog authentication
+
+Authentication is selected explicitly and is independent of the API server's own `API_KEY`.
+
+| Setting | Behavior |
+| --- | --- |
+| `GCP_AUTH_MODE=api_key` (default, including an unset/empty value) | Requires `GCP_API_KEY`; sends only `X-Goog-Api-Key`, never discovers ADC. Existing key-based deployments keep working. |
+| `GCP_AUTH_MODE=adc` | Uses `golang.org/x/oauth2/google.DefaultTokenSource` and a cached, refreshable OAuth token source. Ignores `GCP_API_KEY`, even when ADC fails. |
+| `GCP_QUOTA_PROJECT` (optional) | Sends `X-Goog-User-Project` on both services and SKU calls. Set explicitly when the credential requires a consumer/quota project. Not inferred from gcloud, credential JSON, or a token. Empty means no quota header. Values are validated before any request. |
+
+Other modes fail with a redacted configuration error. The importer requests
+`https://www.googleapis.com/auth/cloud-billing.readonly`, an accepted Cloud Billing
+Catalog scope. Existing user ADC must already have suitable consent/scopes; the
+application cannot broaden an existing refresh token's grant. Broader existing
+`cloud-platform` grants can also authorize catalog reads. Google may require
+Cloud Billing API access and `serviceusage.services.use` on the quota project;
+this application does not enable APIs or modify IAM.
+
+ADC uses Google's standard discovery (configured credential file, provisioned local
+ADC, or an attached identity). Only explicitly choose ADC in a runtime provisioned
+with trusted credentials/configuration. The application does not invoke `gcloud`,
+perform login, copy credentials, or offer a static bearer-token environment variable.
+The SDK owns credential discovery/token exchange; OAuth token requests necessarily
+use Google's auth endpoints or the trusted ADC configuration, not the catalog origin.
+
+## Usage
+
+With ADC already provisioned for this runtime:
+
+```sh
+GCP_AUTH_MODE=adc GCP_QUOTA_PROJECT=my-quota-project ./c3x-pricing-api scrape --vendor gcp
+```
+
+`--vendor all` also honors ADC. Key validation/ADC token acquisition occurs before
+DB connection and migrations; remote API permission/quota errors can only be known
+when the catalog is called. The scraper reuses the preflight source and its full
+scrape-lifetime context for refresh. Initialize a fresh scraper per scrape/probe;
+do not reuse a scraper after its lifetime context is canceled. Worker cancellation
+stops waiting promptly; at most one SDK token acquisition is in flight per scraper.
+SDK OAuth HTTP calls have a 30-second timeout; catalog HTTP calls retain 120 seconds.
+
+Both Compose examples forward the mode/quota settings but intentionally do not
+mount credentials. Operators must provision a suitable identity in the runtime.
+Kubernetes and GitHub Actions examples retain their existing API-key defaults;
+ADC deployments must explicitly add their own identity provisioning and mode/quota
+environment settings. No host home or credential directory is mounted by default.
+
+## Bounded, opt-in probe (no database)
+
+```sh
+go build -o gcp-catalog-probe ./cmd/gcp-catalog-probe
+GCP_AUTH_MODE=adc GCP_QUOTA_PROJECT=my-quota-project ./gcp-catalog-probe --live
+```
+
+The explicit `--live` gate is required. The probe calls the production catalog
+helper once for `services?pageSize=1` and once for Compute Engine
+`services/6F81-5844-456A/skus?pageSize=1`. There are no retries, pagination, database
+operations or product transformations. An overall 60-second deadline applies.
+Successful JSON reports only status and the two counts; errors return nonzero.
+It is a connectivity/auth check, not a catalog-completeness or mapping test.
+`GCPScraper.ProbeCatalog(ctx)` exposes the same bounded operation to Go callers.
+
+## Security and failure semantics
+
+- Catalog credentials are added only after validating the exact origin
+  `https://cloudbilling.googleapis.com` (no custom host/port, userinfo or fragment).
+  Both API-key and ADC requests reject all redirects, including same-origin ones.
+  SDK OAuth HTTP also rejects redirects.
+- Catalog HTTP errors expose only status codes. OAuth/discovery, transport,
+  response-body read and JSON decode errors are redacted; raw remote bodies,
+  headers, URLs, tokens and keys are not returned/logged by the auth/request helpers.
+- ADC acquisition/refresh errors and catalog HTTP 400/401/403 abort the scrape;
+  they cannot be reported as a successful empty import. HTTP 400 is conservatively
+  fatal because Google can use it for an invalid API key. Existing partial-failure
+  behavior for unrelated service errors and bounded SKU retries for network,
+  429 and 5xx errors remain.
+- This change does not alter G4, Flex, Hyperdisk or any product mapping.
+
+## Offline validation
+
+```sh
+go test -short -count=1 ./...
+go test -race -short -count=1 ./...
+go vet ./...
+go build -o c3x-pricing-api ./cmd/server
+```
+
+New tests inject token-source factories and fake `http.RoundTripper`s. They do not
+read ADC files, invoke gcloud, or call the live catalog/token endpoints. Coverage
+includes both endpoint headers, explicit mode selection/no fallback, preflight
+before DB parsing, official OAuth refresh and concurrent cache reuse, lifetime and
+worker cancellation, invalid tokens/quota headers, origin/redirect confinement,
+redacted errors, fatal auth statuses, and the bounded opt-in probe.
+Live ADC verification is a separate operator-controlled step; no test automatically
+uses local credentials. DB integration-tag tests are outside this auth change.
